MESSAGE
is this json valid: {"a":1}

SKILLS (1 is the draft)
1. validateJson — Check whether some JSON parses, and say exactly where the error is if it does not.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "check this json array" → {"text":"[1, 2, 3]"}
2. validateJsonSchema — Check whether a JSON document matches a JSON Schema.
  needs: schema: string, data: string
  e.g. "does this json match the schema" → {"schema":"{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"name\"],\"properties\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}}","data":"{\"name\":\"Ana\"}"}
3. diffJson — Compare two JSON documents and list the paths added, removed and changed.
  needs: left: string, right: string
  e.g. "diff these two json documents" → {"left":"{\"name\":\"Ana\",\"age\":34}","right":"{\"name\":\"Bea\",\"age\":34,\"city\":\"Leeds\"}"}
4. flattenJson — Flatten nested JSON into a single level of dot-separated paths.
  needs: json: string
  optional: separator: string, arrayIndices: boolean
  e.g. "flatten this json" → {"json":"{\"a\":{\"b\":1,\"c\":2}}"}

